  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A vertical forest of aurora-crystal spires rising from the eastern shelf, adjacent to Aurora Stack proper, where bioluminescent krill swarms have been harvested at industrial scale since the Clever Ice Age. The spires were originally cut to channel aurora-light into concentrated beams for ritual use; their facets sang with the sky-glow. That function is now largely vestigial. Half the facets are dark or deliberately dulled, and Slide Prism refineries — which fragment aurora-light into prismatic beams for krill-bloom tracking — run without pause, day-cycle and dark-cycle alike. The krill still come in vast, hypnotic clouds. So do the merchants.
    
    Old Aurora Stack markings survive beneath newer ones. Someone scratched *'Kael remembers'* into a support beam. No one has erased it. No one has explained it, either.
    
    ## Seizure and Succession
    
    Holdborn (ice-thresh), an Aurora splinter faction, seized the Beacon Stack during the consolidation campaigns of the Frozen Peace, claiming authority by right of occupation during the Great Thaw. The bloodstains on the loading docks date to this period. The succession crisis known as Of The First Shelf (ice-wept) — triggered when the Stack's eldest mystic died without naming a successor — fractured Aurora governance into competing claims, each backed by rival readings of the Dawn Mandate. The crisis nearly broke the Flipper Accord itself and left the Nightshelf observing, with some justification, that the sky-dwellers would sooner burn their own crystal reserves than negotiate.
    
    ## The Accord of Beacon Light and Deep Fire
    
    The joint stewardship accord divides governance between Holdborn (ice-thresh), which administers surface operations including harvester platforms and Slide Prism refineries, and the Nightshelf guild Weal' Clique~, which maintains subsurface operations including corruption monitoring and deep-ice stabilization.
    
    | Provision | Detail |
    |---|---|
    | Signatories | Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam (Holdborn); Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ (Weal' Clique~) |
    | Instrument of signing | The fractured ☽'micseleia' Dagger |
    | Crystal harvest quota | Three-fifths surface, two-fifths subsurface |
    | Memorial provision | One-tenth reserved for an extinct household; no surviving claimant |
    | Garrison (Long Dark) | Minimum twelve armed penguins per faction, separate sectors; sealed written authorization required to cross |
    | Enforcement | Courier Corps under Stillness-Bound precedent, four Long Dark cycles |
    | Mutual defense | Obligatory against orca war-pods |
    
    The accord's own language acknowledges that the corruption pressing against the crystal spires — manifestations of Drift-coalesce (glacial), the uncontrolled aurora-crystallization that grows where it should not — can be contained but not cured. Neither signatory names this directly. They committed it to ink all the same.
    
    ## Trade
    
    The Beacon Stack maintains trade relationships with ☽'moth Silvesiris~, a geothermal spring complex in the Nightshelf's southern reaches, and The Frost Zenith. It was active as a strategic resource site during the Orca Incursion, though the details of its wartime role remain poorly documented in sources available to me.
